  "summary": "Preprints tie circuit compilation to physical costs like pulse latency and two-qubit count, alongside scalable classical simulation for near-Clifford and Pauli workloads.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is cost-aware circuit optimization against hardware constraints. SCOPE guides compilation with an operator Schmidt time surrogate to cut pulse execution latency, reporting gains over EPOC on 104 benchmarks. The quspect SDK selects routings after coupling-constrained resynthesis, reaching 0.616x Qiskit O3 two-qubit gates on 55 circuits across five targets. The QAOA Max-Cut work prunes interactions via MinLA surrogates to reduce two-qubit depth, with classical recovery afterward. A deterministic quantum-walk search is realized on a gate-based processor. Adjacent classical-simulation papers, F2-linear partitioning for Pauli propagation and MASQ for near-Clifford error-correction sampling, address verification and scaling. The flow-simulation paper is a looser application-level neighbor, using surface-code resource estimates.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-sonnet-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-18"
}
